  "worked_solution": "If $A\u2286B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $Z\u2286{Z}^{+}$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every integer is a positive integer. For example, we have $-1\\in Z$ but $-1\\notin {Z}^{+}.$",
